      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 & k \\\\ -4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((k)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (3)-(-2)\\cdot (4)))+((8)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (3)-(-2)\\cdot (7)))+((k)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (4)-(-4)\\cdot (7)))\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot (-4))+((8)\\cdot (2))+((k)\\cdot (12))\\\\ &=(8)+(16)+(12k)\\\\ &=12k+24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12k+24&=0\\\\ 12k&=-24\\\\ k&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-2.$",
