      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ k & -6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((0)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -6 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((0)\\cdot ((-6)\\cdot (3)-(0)\\cdot (0)))+((-1)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (3)-(0)\\cdot (2)))+((-2)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (0)-(-6)\\cdot (2)))\\\\ &=((0)\\cdot (-18))+((-1)\\cdot (3k))+((-2)\\cdot (12))\\\\ &=(0)+(-3k)+(-24)\\\\ &=-3k-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3k-24&=0\\\\ -3k&=24\\\\ k&=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-8.$",
