      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -6 \\\\ k^{2} & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|)+((2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 \\\\ k^{2} & 2\\end{aligned}|)+((-8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ k^{2} & 5\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot (2)-(-6)\\cdot (5)))+((2)\\cdot ((5)\\cdot (2)-(-6)\\cdot (k^{2})))+((-8)\\cdot ((5)\\cdot (5)-(-1)\\cdot (k^{2})))\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot (28))+((2)\\cdot (6k^{2}+10))+((-8)\\cdot (k^{2}+25))\\\\ &=(-56)+(12k^{2}+20)+(-8k^{2}-200)\\\\ &=4k^{2}-236\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4k^{2}-236&=0\\\\ 4k^{2}&=236\\\\ k^{2}&=59\\\\ k&=\\pm \\sqrt{59}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\sqrt{59}$ or $k=\\sqrt{59}.$",
