      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & k & k \\\\ 7 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & k \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|)+((-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & k \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}|)+((0)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & k \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((5)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (-4)-(k)\\cdot (8)))+((-1)\\cdot ((8)\\cdot (-4)-(k)\\cdot (7)))+((0)\\cdot ((8)\\cdot (8)-(k)\\cdot (7)))\\\\ &=((5)\\cdot (-12k))+((-1)\\cdot (-7k-32))+((0)\\cdot (64-7k))\\\\ &=(-60k)+(7k+32)+(0)\\\\ &=32-53k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}32-53k&=0\\\\ -53k&=-32\\\\ k&=\\frac{32}{53}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{32}{53}.$",
