      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-8 & -2 & k \\\\ -7 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -6 & 6\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{aligned}|)+((2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}|)+((k)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -6\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-8)\\cdot ((4)\\cdot (6)-(4)\\cdot (-6)))+((2)\\cdot ((-7)\\cdot (6)-(4)\\cdot (-4)))+((k)\\cdot ((-7)\\cdot (-6)-(4)\\cdot (-4)))\\\\ &=((-8)\\cdot (48))+((2)\\cdot (-26))+((k)\\cdot (58))\\\\ &=(-384)+(-52)+(58k)\\\\ &=58k-436\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}58k-436&=0\\\\ 58k&=436\\\\ k&=\\frac{218}{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{218}{29}.$",
