    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e004a3e4-1534-5b3e-a82f-cb002cf57e1d",
      ":question/problem": "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=\u27e82,-2,-2\u27e9$, $b=\u27e82,4,k^{2}\u27e9$, and $c=\u27e8-1,-2,-2\u27e9$ are coplanar.\n\n**In ascending order:**\n\n$k=${{field-1}}\nand\n$k=${{field-2}}",
