      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ k & 7 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}|)+((-8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}|)+((1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 7 \\\\ -3 & -8\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot ((7)\\cdot (4)-(2)\\cdot (-8)))+((-8)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (4)-(2)\\cdot (-3)))+((1)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (-8)-(7)\\cdot (-3)))\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot (44))+((-8)\\cdot (4k+6))+((1)\\cdot (21-8k))\\\\ &=(-88)+(-32k-48)+(21-8k)\\\\ &=-40k-115\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-40k-115&=0\\\\ -40k&=115\\\\ k&=-\\frac{23}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{23}{8}.$",
