      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}8 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 6 & k & k\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 \\\\ k & k\\end{aligned}|)+((7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ 6 & k\\end{aligned}|)+((3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & k\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot ((8)\\cdot (k)-(-5)\\cdot (k)))+((7)\\cdot ((6)\\cdot (k)-(-5)\\cdot (6)))+((3)\\cdot ((6)\\cdot (k)-(8)\\cdot (6)))\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot (13k))+((7)\\cdot (6k+30))+((3)\\cdot (6k-48))\\\\ &=(104k)+(42k+210)+(18k-144)\\\\ &=164k+66\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}164k+66&=0\\\\ 164k&=-66\\\\ k&=-\\frac{33}{82}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{33}{82}.$",
