      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ k & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 8\\end{aligned}|)+((-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ k & 8\\end{aligned}|)+((-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ k & -8\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-1)\\cdot ((3)\\cdot (8)-(0)\\cdot (-8)))+((-1)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (8)-(0)\\cdot (k)))+((-2)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (-8)-(3)\\cdot (k)))\\\\ &=((-1)\\cdot (24))+((-1)\\cdot (-32))+((-2)\\cdot (32-3k))\\\\ &=(-24)+(32)+(6k-64)\\\\ &=6k-56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6k-56&=0\\\\ 6k&=56\\\\ k&=\\frac{28}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{28}{3}.$",
